<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Dignity of the Human Person" cic="CCC 1700-1715" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Section 1: Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<p>Answer from your memory of the lesson, then check your answers against the Catechism.</p>

<ol>
  <li>What does the book of Genesis say about the creation of the human being? Quote the verse.</li>
  <li>What three faculties make us &laquo;in the image of God,&raquo; according to the Catechism?</li>
  <li>What consequences did original sin have on human dignity &mdash; and what did it NOT do?</li>
  <li>What does it mean that the human being is a unity of body and soul?</li>
  <li>What did St. Leo the Great tell newly baptized Christians about their dignity?</li>
  <li>According to <em>Gaudium et Spes</em> 22, what does Christ do for man?</li>
  <li>Name the four pillars of Catholic social teaching that flow from human dignity.</li>
  <li>What four modern errors attack human dignity, according to the lesson?</li>
</ol>
</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Section 2: For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions &mdash; only honest ones.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What really makes you feel valuable? Where does your sense of self-worth come from?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think about the voices you hear when you evaluate yourself. Are they the world's voices or God's voice? What would change if you grounded your self-worth in being created in the image of God?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Is there someone you find it difficult to treat with dignity? Why?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">It could be someone who has hurt you, someone whose views you despise, or someone you simply ignore because they seem unimportant. What would it mean to see the image of God in them?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. The wound of original sin. In what area of your life do you feel an &laquo;interior division&raquo; most strongly?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">St. Paul described it: &laquo;I do not do the good I want, but the evil I do not want is what I do&raquo; (Rom 7:19). Where do you experience that tension between who you want to be and what you actually do?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. What would change in your life if you truly believed you were a child of God with infinite dignity?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Be concrete: a decision you would make, a conversation you would have, a habit you would change. Name at least two things.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. &laquo;Christ reveals man to man himself.&raquo; What do you learn about yourself when you look at Jesus?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Jesus is perfectly free, perfectly self-giving, perfectly merciful. What does his way of being human teach you about your own humanity and vocation?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">6. How can you recognize and defend the dignity of the people around you this week?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">In your family, your workplace, your school, your community. Name three concrete actions.</p>
